    "complexity_is_proportional": false,
    "rationale": "Rejected: coalescing coefficient preparation plus six HT/packet submissions into two total command buffers improved the 512x512 cell but regressed 128x128 by 5.90%. Separate compute encoders and barriers were preserved. No uniform end-to-end gain warrants a new size heuristic. Production submission behavior restored; profiling/codestream parity checks retained. Corpus uses patterned_rgb8, batch 16, 3 decomposition levels, 64x64 blocks; initial private upload and final CPU readback excluded from timing. Input hashes frame each RGB8 tile with its little-endian u64 byte length, then concatenate all 16 tiles; the environment hash identifies the 512x512 priority cell. Commands and additional limitations are in P20-metal-optimization-notes.md. Temporary A/B environment switches removed after the experiment."
